WEBVTT

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.030
Strike!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.120
Oh no, the count is 3-2! Sanders is cornered!

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.600
Strike out!

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.520
Sanders was struck out!

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.470
The Bats miss their chance to put the game out of reach in this inning too.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.980
Don't swing at such a weak pitch!

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.460
All right! A one-run difference in the last inning.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.890
Let's rally and win right away in this inning!

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.360
Attention please, now pitching, number 56:

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.430
Goro Shigeno!

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.880
Come at me with all you've got!

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.330
<i>Closer!?</i>

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:27.990
<i>Yes.</i>

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.830
<i>As the Bats are right now, we need a reliable closer.</i>

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.210
<i>And therefore, I want to entrust you with that task, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.710
<i>If you become our closer, we can realistically aim for victory this time! That's why-</i>

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.190
<i>I refuse.</i>

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.580
<i>You think I could stand being a closer?</i>

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.850
<i>If you're a pitcher, you should pitch the whole game!</i>

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.090
<i>You should know that I'm a pitcher that pitches with all I've got from the start.</i>

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.410
<i>Shigeno-kun, you're surprisingly old-fashioned.</i>

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.820
<i>W-What?</i>

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.320
<i>Every game, it's a serious battle to not allow even one run.</i>

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:07.050
<i>No matter how outnumbered you are, if you step onto the mound, you have to hold the opponent back.</i>

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.040
<i>It's truly correct to call it the team's fortress.</i>

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:15.300
<i>Well, if you can't handle that pressure, the matter is different.</i>

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.460
<i>Hey! Who said that!?</i>

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.700
<i>Do I have that much pressure on me?</i>

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.810
<i>Closer? Just what I wanted!</i>

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.020
<i>I'll take it on!</i>

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.610
<i>That little girl, she says whatever she pleases.</i>

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.850
<i>As long as I hold them back,</i>

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.240
<i>there isn't a problem!</i>

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.790
Strike!

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.540
What...

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.260
is that Asian?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.550
Nice pitch, Shigeno-kun!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.310
<i>With this pitch, it's over!</i>

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.350
Strike out! Game over!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.270
He struck out all three players.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.950
You did it!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.450
You did it, Shigeno!

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:17.020
You really are the best!

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.830
Stop it, old man! That's disgusting!

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.040
Don't be shy!

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.660
Let go of me, you geezer! I'll fall!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.930
Hi! Hello, everybody!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.650
Today we're reporting from the Tokyo Warriors' camp in Miyazaki.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.700
This year's big sensation was...

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.870
drafted at number one from Kaido High School-
an able player right from the start.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.710
And to top it off, he's really good looking too!

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:09.950
Hey!

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.830
Ta-da! Rod-chan is here!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.920
Stop it, Rodman-san, you're in the way!

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.320
Please move!

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.040
Toshi-kun! Don't move!

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.340
Oh, it seems like Sato's batting practice is starting!

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.870
<i>I've finally made it here:</i>

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.800
<i>the pro world that I've been dreaming about!</i>

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.890
<i>With this I can repay my grandfather and grandmother!</i>

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.520
He's sure hitting it far.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.910
Just what you'd expect from the genius rookie.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.890
He's hitting it nicely.

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:53.950
Yeah.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.150
He trained hard in the off-season.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.710
It looks like his body has developed along with his skill.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.420
He might even be a starter when the curtain rises.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.520
<i>Those people...</i>

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.810
You're in the way!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.620
Y-Yatabe-san!

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.110
You're here looking for material for another stupid article again, aren't you?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.590
You don't have to say it that way!

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:30.530
If you've got time to do things like that, you might as well help with ground maintenance.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.690
Let's go.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:33.920
Yeah.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.320
Yatabe-san!

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:38.090
Good morning!

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.430
Don't take your eyes off the ball.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.610
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.080
Yatabe-san, good morning!

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.100
Morning!

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.410
Good morning!

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.930
Oh! How're you feeling?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.130
So-so.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.610
What do you mean, so-so?

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:57.260
As usual, he's only cold towards Sato.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.530
Yeah, maybe.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.910
"Maybe"?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.950
You don't think the old guy is afraid?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.690
That his star status might be stolen by Sato?

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.010
Aota!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.600
It was just a joke... A joke!

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.490
Don't take it seriously.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.820
Thank you very much!

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:14.330
Sato!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.500
Y-Yes?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.050
In tomorrow's Red-White game, you'll wear the starting catcher's mask for the White team!

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.080
The pitcher will be Kamihira.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.750
I'm going to form a battery with Kamihira-san, the ace?

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.590
Isn't that great, Sato?

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.980
It's your chance to show off your skills!

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.220
Y-Yes!

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:40.640
Coach Araki!

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.810
Can I borrow some video and the scorebook from last year?

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:48.090
What? Um, sure. I don't mind.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.430
Thank you!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:08:00.530
And then, Tanioka received a present that was <i>this</i> huge, and he was floating on pink clouds!

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.390
And then that girl was all, "P-Please give this to Toshi-kun"!

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.850
When I picture Tanioka's face then, I...

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.230
It couldn't be helped!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.520
I haven't received something like that since I was a rookie!

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.090
How sad!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.520
Shut up!

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.220
Well? What was in it?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.640
Well... it was...

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.970
A stuffed panda, wasn't it?

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.930
How did you know?

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.060
A panda, huh?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:28.700
This guy is going all "Pan-chan" in his room!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.050
You cute boy.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.330
I'm telling you that I don't do things like that!

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:39.370
Well, we each have our own tastes.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.160
Even you're saying that, Uchimura-san!

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:43.070
Are you running away?

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:45.280
I'm telling you, that's not the case.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.350
Hey!

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.300
We've got a gift from our local fans: mangoes!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.090
Mango!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.040
Time to eat!

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.430
This is the best!

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:51.820
We are now beginning the Tokyo Warriors' Red-White game.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.900
Toshi-kun, do your best!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:00.490
Top of the first inning: leading off for the Red team...

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.170
Batting first: left fielder, Aota.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.540
Just what you'd expect when the genius rookie debuts in a real game.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.980
Lots of girls have come to watch.

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:11.630
Aota-san.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.570
If you hit the ball, they'll hate you.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.260
That'd be a problem.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.720
Well, for now, can you show me...

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.660
how the genius rookie leads?

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.140
Play!

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.670
<i>Kamihira-san gets uneasy at the beginning of games.</i>

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:31.810
<i>I have to take special care that the quick Aota-san doesn't get on base.</i>

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.790
<i>Everyone... What a level of concentration!</i>

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:48.900
<i>Is this what the pros are?</i>

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.480
<i>Is this the tension of the pros?</i>

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:55.180
<i>It seems like it's best not to try to get a strike right away, since it won't be easy.</i>

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.530
<i>First, we'll...</i>

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.140
Strike!

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:07.430
A ball, huh?

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.020
<i>This is Kamihira-san's ball.</i>

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.080
<i>He throws it so well, even now.</i>

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.440
<i>True to his reputation.</i>

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.690
<i>Okay! This time, we'll...</i>

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.070
Strike two!

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.000
It isn't coming where I want it.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.240
<i>Even Aota-san can't do anything against this pitch when it's in this location.</i>

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:29.970
<i>Okay!</i>

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:32.710
<i>Then we'll challenge him for the third strike!</i>

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:41.420
Safe!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.140
Well done, Aota!

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.470
Nice bunt!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.970
<i>I can't believe he'd bunt with it 0-2.</i>

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.020
<i>No, this is my mistake.</i>

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:56.820
<i>I got so preoccupied with Aota-san that I didn't notice Uchimura-san behind him looking worried.</i>

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.300
<i>Concentrate.</i>

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.360
<i>Concentrate!</i>

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.990
This is a free fansub.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.990
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:15.100
Batting second: second baseman, Kidokoro.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.080
Play!

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.520
<i>No outs, and a runner on first base.</i>

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.880
<i>He'll most likely try to sacrifice bunt here.</i>

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.030
<i>But...</i>

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:24.980
<i>if I take Aota-san's legs into consideration,</i>

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:26.860
<i>it's very likely that he'll try to steal a base.</i>

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.860
<i>For the time being, let's have the first pitch miss and study the situation.</i>

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.100
It's a duel between Aota's legs and Sato's arm.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.170
This'll be a sight to see!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:41.860
Ball!

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.820
<i>He's not going to run?</i>

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:46.960
<i>What will he do next? A sacrifice bunt?</i>

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.280
<i>Which one?</i>

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:52.580
<i>At any rate, if Aota-san is going to run, we'll raise the count first.</i>

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.710
<i>He's taking a bigger lead than before.</i>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.670
<i>Is he going to go for it?</i>

00:12:58.910 --> 00:12:59.640
<i>He is!</i>

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:02.760
Ball!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:08.800
Hey, Kurogome, isn't Sato being too cautious?

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.970
It's Aota's legs; a rookie sees them as a threat.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:14.160
<i>Bunt!?</i>

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.810
<i>No, he's faking, so Aota-san can run again.</i>

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.480
<i>If we go for a strike here, in the worst case scenario, he'll sacrifice bunt.</i>

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.780
<i>It doesn't matter if it gets to one out with a runner on second.</i>

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:25.750
<i>Wha-</i>

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.120
Nice batting!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.390
Okay! This is good!

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:34.920
Keep it going!

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.460
<i>You've still got a way to go.</i>

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:41.590
<i>It was clear it'd come to this when you easily fell into a no out, two on situation.</i>

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:45.300
Batting third: first baseman, Rodman.

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:48.770
Hey, cute boy! Let's get along.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.060
<i>No outs, and a runner on first and second.</i>

00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:00.440
<i>Okay, here we'll get him to hit a ball that's in the middle and low and get the double play!</i>

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.540
Damn it!

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.240
Thank you, Sato.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:19.330
Safe!

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.640
That was dangerous!

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:29.880
Cute boy, your ball almost hit me! Please be more careful, okay?

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.790
Are you implying that what I'm saying is false?

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.440
I apologize.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.780
Because of my mistake, they were able to score two runs on us.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.980
Don't worry about it. We'll get them back for sure.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.650
Yeah...

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.780
There's no need to pout like that!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.950
The real game starts now, right?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.360
Y-Yes!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.350
To first!

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.800
Safe! Safe!

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.270
That wasn't Kamihira's fault.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.560
His pitching has a good edge to it; it's not bad.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:27.330
Is the problem Sato's lead?

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:32.110
It's the pressure of the pros, isn't it? It's his first real game after all.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.870
Batting seventh: catcher, Yatabe.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:43.370
<i>With no outs, a runner on second and third, Yatabe-san comes up.</i>

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:47.670
<i>His batting average is only .200, but he's strong when there are runners in scoring position.</i>

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.180
<i>Taking the next batter into consideration,
there's no reason to challenge him head on.</i>

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.430
<i>We'll try to use a sneaky pitch here.
In the worst case scenario, we'll walk him.</i>

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.350
Ball! {Though it sounds like it could be Foul too}

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.360
You're timid.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.120
Getting all the way to me, the seventh batter,
in the first inning and going with a bases-loaded strategy...

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:14.410
Is that Kaido's baseball manual?

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:18.240
Kaido's baseball isn't all that great after all.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:26.040
Well, for a team that can't win if they can't crush their opponent's pitcher, I guess that's all they can do.

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.880
Yatabe-san!

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.200
<i>You're wrong!</i>

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.400
<i>Our baseball isn't like that!</i>

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:42.600
<i>I'll get you out for everyone's sake!</i>

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:47.080
<i>First, we'll attack Yatabe-san's weakness. A rising pitch down the middle on the first pitch!</i>

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:00.580
Safe!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.750
Nice batting!

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:16.050
<i>It can't be that Yatabe-san said that on purpose to agitate me!</i>

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:17.540
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.050
<i>Why did I get drawn in by that provocation?</i>

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:22.890
<i>I just had to think a bit, and I would have understood that!</i>

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.320
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:30.020
Batting eighth: right fielder, Yoshioka.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:35.450
<i>If I remember correctly, Yoshioka-san has a habit of letting the first pitch go if it's a breaking ball.</i>

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:37.950
<i>We'll start with a curve that moves away...</i>

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.610
<i>and raise the count!</i>

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.950
Center!

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:49.380
Out!

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:54.170
One out! One out!

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.550
Out!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.850
Out!

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.520
Kamihira-san!

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:11.160
I apologize.

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.590
I'm sorry for my worthless lead.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:14.980
Don't worry about it.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:20.000
My balls aren't as sharp as they usually are either due to camp being at its peak.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.700
Also, this is a Red-White game.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.550
It isn't the real deal.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.180
Ball!

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:35.990
Ball!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.590
Ball! Ball four!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.930
Okay! No outs with a runner on!

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.890
Tanioka! Slide!

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:48.730
Kurai! Don't mind, don't mind. Gather strength from this failure for the next pitch.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:48.730
Batting second: second baseman, Tanioka.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:52.360
<i>No outs and the runner is the swift Miura-san.</i>

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.770
<i>It's the same situation as the upper half of the inning.</i>

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.570
<i>What kind of lead will Yatabe-san use?</i>

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.830
To first!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.500
Out!

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.540
<i>He managed to deal with a sacrifice bunt situation so easily.</i>

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.670
<i>What in the world is Yatabe-san?</i>

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:18.840
Out!

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.380
<i>I see! They've got six runs!</i>

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:27.130
<i>First, he'll make sure to get some outs to let the pitcher get a grasp on the pace.</i>

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.860
Out!

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:30.910
Okay!

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.410
Well done, Kurai!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.050
<i>That was excellent.</i>

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:38.820
<i>He skillfully controlled Kurai-san, who has trouble at the beginning of games!</i>

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.330
I don't know about this.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.170
Sato isn't standing out at all.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.700
And his defense in the first inning was full of holes too.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:55.650
Yeah.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:20:00.220
And he struck out twice, was walked, and hit into a double play once as well.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.550
Strike! Batter out!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.380
I guess the star is still Yatabe, huh?

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:12.020
Batting seventh: catcher, Sato.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.870
Go for it, Toshi-kun!

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.980
We'll count on you to hit a big one, Sato!

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.850
<i>I can't let it end like this!</i>

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.190
<i>I'll help us tie it in some way!</i>

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.710
Aren't you straining yourself too much?

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.660
Well then, where will the pitch come from?

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.740
<i>Don't let him provoke you!</i>

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.160
<i>Concentrate!</i>

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:37.190
<i>Sakada-san's out-pitch is a slider with good movement.</i>

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.130
<i>Most likely his first pitch will be a fastball.</i>

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:43.510
Strike!

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.560
<i>He used the slider right away!?</i>

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:47.280
<i>The next one will be high and inside...</i>

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.680
<i>or maybe another slider outside?</i>

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.480
Foul!

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.420
<i>A slider again on the second pitch?</i>

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:04.790
<i>Again!</i>

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:13.450
Safe!

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.750
He followed that nicely!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.880
He's doing quite well!

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:29.220
Batting eighth: second baseman, Tsukioka.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.520
<i>If I get home, it'll tie it up.</i>

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:37.190
<i>Their defense isn't shallow enough that I can easily do that.</i>

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.690
<i>If the ball gets out of the infield, I'll score that one run!</i>

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:04.090
Sato! Don't look around and just slide!

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:16.850
Out!

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.160
Pathetic.

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:29.090
Playing half-heartedly because you're scared?

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:34.290
You're not a pro!

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.980
Pining for the polished play of a pro right away,

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.890
Toshiya is depressed.

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:17.670
An exhibition game is scheduled during that period.

00:24:17.670 --> 00:24:19.830
Don't just stay depressed!

00:24:19.830 --> 00:24:21.440
If it's you, you can do much better than that!

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:22.940
Get a hold of yourself, Toshiya!

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:24.690
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:25.480
Challenger.

00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:28.290
Run to the stage of your dreams!
